  "description": "An empty USRSEC on a first entry: STARTBR's WHEN DFHRESP(NOTFND) arm at :600-606. No key is at or after LOW-VALUES because the file holds no record, so the browse never opens. The arm opens with a bare CONTINUE, and the statements after it DO execute - USER-SEC-EOF is set, 'You are at the top of the page...' is painted and the map is sent - which is the single easiest thing to get wrong here. It raises no error flag, so :286 still admits the rest of PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD: :288 is false for ENTER so no record is discarded, :292's guard fails so the ten rows keep the spaces :117 left them at, the loop at :300 never iterates, and in the ELSE at :317-322 WS-IDX is still 1 so the page number is NOT incremented and stays 00000000. That zero is the assertion: an empty file leaves the operator on page zero, not page one.",
